--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
NAMING DECISION (documented drift — Honesty Covenant #9 "no silent drift")
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The source prompt's generated native target is `modals-dialogs/ConfirmDialog.*`. That path is
ALREADY OWNED by a different, already-shipped surface: P4/modals-dialogs/0012, the native parity of
web `components/ui/ConfirmDialog.tsx` (the destructive-action confirm dialog with typed-confirmation
gate + "Don't ask again" silence). THIS prompt (0001) targets a DIFFERENT web component —
`components/ai/ConfirmDialog.tsx`, exported as `AiConfirmDialog` — the Helix AI tool-use approval
dialog. The generator collided the two because both .tsx files share the basename `ConfirmDialog`.

Writing to `ConfirmDialog.*` would OVERWRITE and destroy the completed 0012 surface (covenant #7
"no predecessor bypass"). Resolution: this AI variant ships as `AiConfirmDialog.*` — types prefixed
`AiConfirm*`, strings table "AiConfirmDialog", diagnostics slug "AiConfirmDialog" — matching the web
component's exported name `AiConfirmDialog` and the established `Ai*` native convention
(AiOutputPanel, AiLimitBanner, AiUsageCard). No collision with 0012; both surfaces coexist.

project.yml and .swiftlint.yml are NOT edited (covenant #9): the ENTIRE `modals-dialogs/` tier
(~30 surfaces incl. 0012) is deliberately not yet wired into the Xcode project — the same state the
0012 predecessor committed (its log: "project.yml ... UNCHANGED"). Tier integration is a separate
P4 acceptance step; touching it is outside this prompt's Allowed-files scope and would risk ~30
unrelated sibling surfaces.

